NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000001 "package File::ShareDir;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000002 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000003 "=pod"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000004 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000005 "=head1 NAME"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000006 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000007 "File::ShareDir - Locate per-dist and per-module shared files"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000008 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000009 "=begin html"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000010 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000011 "<a href=\"https://travis-ci.org/perl5-utils/File-ShareDir\"><img src=\"https://travis-ci.org/perl5-utils/File-ShareDir.svg?branch=master\" alt=\"Travis CI\"/></a>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000012 "<a href='https://coveralls.io/github/perl5-utils/File-ShareDir?branch=master'><img src='https://coveralls.io/repos/github/perl5-utils/File-ShareDir/badge.svg?branch=master' alt='Coverage Status' /></a>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000013 "<a href=\"https://saythanks.io/to/rehsack\"><img src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/Say%20Thanks-!-1EAEDB.svg\" alt=\"Say Thanks\" /></a>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000014 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000015 "=end html"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000016 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000017 "=head1 SYNOPSIS"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000018 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000019 "  use File::ShareDir ':ALL';"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000020 "  "
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000021 "  # Where are distribution-level shared data files kept"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000022 "  $dir = dist_dir('File-ShareDir');"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000023 "  "
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000024 "  # Where are module-level shared data files kept"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000025 "  $dir = module_dir('File::ShareDir');"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000026 "  "
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000027 "  # Find a specific file in our dist/module shared dir"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000028 "  $file = dist_file(  'File-ShareDir',  'file/name.txt');"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000029 "  $file = module_file('File::ShareDir', 'file/name.txt');"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000030 "  "
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000031 "  # Like module_file, but search up the inheritance tree"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000032 "  $file = class_file( 'Foo::Bar', 'file/name.txt' );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000033 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000034 "=head1 DESCRIPTION"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000035 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000036 "The intent of L<File::ShareDir> is to provide a companion to"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000037 "L<Class::Inspector> and L<File::HomeDir>, modules that take a"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000038 "process that is well-known by advanced Perl developers but gets a"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000039 "little tricky, and make it more available to the larger Perl community."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000040 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000041 "Quite often you want or need your Perl module (CPAN or otherwise)"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000042 "to have access to a large amount of read-only data that is stored"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000043 "on the file-system at run-time."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000044 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000045 "On a linux-like system, this would be in a place such as /usr/share,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000046 "however Perl runs on a wide variety of different systems, and so"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000047 "the use of any one location is unreliable."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000048 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000049 "Perl provides a little-known method for doing this, but almost"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000050 "nobody is aware that it exists. As a result, module authors often"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000051 "go through some very strange ways to make the data available to"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000052 "their code."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000053 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000054 "The most common of these is to dump the data out to an enormous"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000055 "Perl data structure and save it into the module itself. The"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000056 "result are enormous multi-megabyte .pm files that chew up a"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000057 "lot of memory needlessly."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000058 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000059 "Another method is to put the data \"file\" after the __DATA__ compiler"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000060 "tag and limit yourself to access as a filehandle."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000061 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000062 "The problem to solve is really quite simple."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000063 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000064 "  1. Write the data files to the system at install time."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000065 "  "
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000066 "  2. Know where you put them at run-time."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000067 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000068 "Perl's install system creates an \"auto\" directory for both"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000069 "every distribution and for every module file."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000070 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000071 "These are used by a couple of different auto-loading systems"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000072 "to store code fragments generated at install time, and various"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000073 "other modules written by the Perl \"ancient masters\"."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000074 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000075 "But the same mechanism is available to any dist or module to"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000076 "store any sort of data."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000077 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000078 "=head2 Using Data in your Module"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000079 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000080 "C<File::ShareDir> forms one half of a two part solution."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000081 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000082 "Once the files have been installed to the correct directory,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000083 "you can use C<File::ShareDir> to find your files again after"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000084 "the installation."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000085 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000086 "For the installation half of the solution, see L<File::ShareDir::Install>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000087 "and its C<install_share> directive."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000088 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000089 "Using L<File::ShareDir::Install> together with L<File::ShareDir>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000090 "allows one to rely on the files in appropriate C<dist_dir()>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000091 "or C<module_dir()> in development phase, too."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000092 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000093 "=head1 FUNCTIONS"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000094 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000095 "C<File::ShareDir> provides four functions for locating files and"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000096 "directories."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000097 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000098 "For greater maintainability, none of these are exported by default"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000099 "and you are expected to name the ones you want at use-time, or provide"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000100 "the C<':ALL'> tag. All of the following are equivalent."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000101 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000102 "  # Load but don't import, and then call directly"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000103 "  use File::ShareDir;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000104 "  $dir = File::ShareDir::dist_dir('My-Dist');"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000105 "  "
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000106 "  # Import a single function"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000107 "  use File::ShareDir 'dist_dir';"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000108 "  dist_dir('My-Dist');"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000109 "  "
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000110 "  # Import all the functions"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000111 "  use File::ShareDir ':ALL';"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000112 "  dist_dir('My-Dist');"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000113 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000114 "All of the functions will check for you that the dir/file actually"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000115 "exists, and that you have read permissions, or they will throw an"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000116 "exception."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000117 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000118 "=cut"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000119 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000120 "use 5.005;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000121 "use strict;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000122 "use warnings;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000123 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000124 "use base ('Exporter');"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000125 "use constant IS_MACOS => !!($^O eq 'MacOS');"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000126 "use constant IS_WIN32 => !!($^O eq 'MSWin32');"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000127 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000128 "use Carp             ();"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000129 "use Exporter         ();"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000130 "use File::Spec       ();"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000131 "use Class::Inspector ();"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000132 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000133 "our %DIST_SHARE;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000134 "our %MODULE_SHARE;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000135 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000136 "our @CARP_NOT;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000137 "our @EXPORT_OK = qw{"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000138 "  dist_dir"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000139 "  dist_file"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000140 "  module_dir"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000141 "  module_file"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000142 "  class_dir"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000143 "  class_file"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000144 "};"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000145 "our %EXPORT_TAGS = ("
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000146 "    ALL => [@EXPORT_OK],"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000147 ");"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000148 "our $VERSION = '1.118';"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000149 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000150 "#####################################################################"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000151 "# Interface Functions"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000152 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000153 "=pod"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000154 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000155 "=head2 dist_dir"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000156 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000157 "  # Get a distribution's shared files directory"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000158 "  my $dir = dist_dir('My-Distribution');"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000159 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000160 "The C<dist_dir> function takes a single parameter of the name of an"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000161 "installed (CPAN or otherwise) distribution, and locates the shared"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000162 "data directory created at install time for it."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000163 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000164 "Returns the directory path as a string, or dies if it cannot be"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000165 "located or is not readable."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000166 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000167 "=cut"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000168 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000169 "sub dist_dir"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000170 "{"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000171 "    my $dist = _DIST(shift);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000172 "    my $dir;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000173 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000174 "    # Try the new version, then fall back to the legacy version"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000175 "    $dir = _dist_dir_new($dist) || _dist_dir_old($dist);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000176 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000177 "    return $dir if defined $dir;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000178 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000179 "    # Ran out of options"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000180 "    Carp::croak(\"Failed to find share dir for dist '$dist'\");"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000181 "}"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000182 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000183 "sub _dist_dir_new"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000184 "{"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000185 "    my $dist = shift;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000186 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000187 "    return $DIST_SHARE{$dist} if exists $DIST_SHARE{$dist};"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000188 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000189 "    # Create the subpath"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000190 "    my $path = File::Spec->catdir('auto', 'share', 'dist', $dist);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000191 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000192 "    # Find the full dir within @INC"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000193 "    return _search_inc_path($path);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000194 "}"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000195 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000196 "sub _dist_dir_old"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000197 "{"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000198 "    my $dist = shift;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000199 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000200 "    # Create the subpath"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000201 "    my $path = File::Spec->catdir('auto', split(/-/, $dist),);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000202 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000203 "    # Find the full dir within @INC"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000204 "    return _search_inc_path($path);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000205 "}"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000206 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000207 "=pod"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000208 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000209 "=head2 module_dir"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000210 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000211 "  # Get a module's shared files directory"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000212 "  my $dir = module_dir('My::Module');"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000213 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000214 "The C<module_dir> function takes a single parameter of the name of an"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000215 "installed (CPAN or otherwise) module, and locates the shared data"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000216 "directory created at install time for it."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000217 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000218 "In order to find the directory, the module B<must> be loaded when"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000219 "calling this function."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000220 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000221 "Returns the directory path as a string, or dies if it cannot be"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000222 "located or is not readable."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000223 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000224 "=cut"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000225 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000226 "sub module_dir"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000227 "{"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000228 "    my $module = _MODULE(shift);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000229 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000230 "    return $MODULE_SHARE{$module} if exists $MODULE_SHARE{$module};"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000231 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000232 "    # Try the new version first, then fall back to the legacy version"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000233 "    return _module_dir_new($module) || _module_dir_old($module);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000234 "}"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000235 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000236 "sub _module_dir_new"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000237 "{"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000238 "    my $module = shift;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000239 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000240 "    # Create the subpath"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000241 "    my $path = File::Spec->catdir('auto', 'share', 'module', _module_subdir($module),);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000242 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000243 "    # Find the full dir within @INC"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000244 "    return _search_inc_path($path);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000245 "}"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000246 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000247 "sub _module_dir_old"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000248 "{"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000249 "    my $module = shift;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000250 "    my $short  = Class::Inspector->filename($module);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000251 "    my $long   = Class::Inspector->loaded_filename($module);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000252 "    $short =~ tr{/}{:}   if IS_MACOS;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000253 "    $short =~ tr{\\\\} {/} if IS_WIN32;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000254 "    $long  =~ tr{\\\\} {/} if IS_WIN32;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000255 "    substr($short, -3, 3, '');"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000256 "    $long =~ m/^(.*)\\Q$short\\E\\.pm\\z/s or Carp::croak(\"Failed to find base dir\");"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000257 "    my $dir = File::Spec->catdir(\"$1\", 'auto', $short);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000258 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000259 "    -d $dir or Carp::croak(\"Directory '$dir': No such directory\");"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000260 "    -r $dir or Carp::croak(\"Directory '$dir': No read permission\");"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000261 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000262 "    return $dir;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000263 "}"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000264 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000265 "=pod"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000266 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000267 "=head2 dist_file"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000268 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000269 "  # Find a file in our distribution shared dir"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000270 "  my $dir = dist_file('My-Distribution', 'file/name.txt');"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000271 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000272 "The C<dist_file> function takes two parameters of the distribution name"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000273 "and file name, locates the dist directory, and then finds the file within"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000274 "it, verifying that the file actually exists, and that it is readable."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000275 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000276 "The filename should be a relative path in the format of your local"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000277 "filesystem. It will simply added to the directory using L<File::Spec>'s"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000278 "C<catfile> method."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000279 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000280 "Returns the file path as a string, or dies if the file or the dist's"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000281 "directory cannot be located, or the file is not readable."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000282 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000283 "=cut"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000284 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000285 "sub dist_file"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000286 "{"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000287 "    my $dist = _DIST(shift);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000288 "    my $file = _FILE(shift);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000289 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000290 "    # Try the new version first, in doubt hand off to the legacy version"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000291 "    my $path = _dist_file_new($dist, $file) || _dist_file_old($dist, $file);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000292 "    $path or Carp::croak(\"Failed to find shared file '$file' for dist '$dist'\");"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000293 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000294 "    -f $path or Carp::croak(\"File '$path': No such file\");"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000295 "    -r $path or Carp::croak(\"File '$path': No read permission\");"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000296 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000297 "    return $path;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000298 "}"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000299 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000300 "sub _dist_file_new"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000301 "{"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000302 "    my $dist = shift;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000303 "    my $file = shift;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000304 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000305 "    # If it exists, what should the path be"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000306 "    my $dir = _dist_dir_new($dist);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000307 "    return undef unless defined $dir;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000308 "    my $path = File::Spec->catfile($dir, $file);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000309 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000310 "    # Does the file exist"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000311 "    return undef unless -e $path;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000312 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000313 "    return $path;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000314 "}"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000315 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000316 "sub _dist_file_old"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000317 "{"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000318 "    my $dist = shift;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000319 "    my $file = shift;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000320 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000321 "    # If it exists, what should the path be"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000322 "    my $dir = _dist_dir_old($dist);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000323 "    return undef unless defined $dir;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000324 "    my $path = File::Spec->catfile($dir, $file);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000325 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000326 "    # Does the file exist"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000327 "    return undef unless -e $path;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000328 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000329 "    return $path;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000330 "}"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000331 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000332 "=pod"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000333 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000334 "=head2 module_file"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000335 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000336 "  # Find a file in our module shared dir"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000337 "  my $dir = module_file('My::Module', 'file/name.txt');"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000338 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000339 "The C<module_file> function takes two parameters of the module name"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000340 "and file name. It locates the module directory, and then finds the file"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000341 "within it, verifying that the file actually exists, and that it is readable."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000342 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000343 "In order to find the directory, the module B<must> be loaded when"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000344 "calling this function."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000345 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000346 "The filename should be a relative path in the format of your local"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000347 "filesystem. It will simply added to the directory using L<File::Spec>'s"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000348 "C<catfile> method."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000349 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000350 "Returns the file path as a string, or dies if the file or the dist's"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000351 "directory cannot be located, or the file is not readable."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000352 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000353 "=cut"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000354 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000355 "sub module_file"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000356 "{"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000357 "    my $module = _MODULE(shift);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000358 "    my $file   = _FILE(shift);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000359 "    my $dir    = module_dir($module);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000360 "    my $path   = File::Spec->catfile($dir, $file);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000361 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000362 "    -e $path or Carp::croak(\"File '$path' does not exist in module dir\");"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000363 "    -r $path or Carp::croak(\"File '$path': No read permission\");"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000364 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000365 "    return $path;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000366 "}"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000367 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000368 "=pod"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000369 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000370 "=head2 class_file"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000371 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000372 "  # Find a file in our module shared dir, or in our parent class"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000373 "  my $dir = class_file('My::Module', 'file/name.txt');"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000374 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000375 "The C<module_file> function takes two parameters of the module name"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000376 "and file name. It locates the module directory, and then finds the file"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000377 "within it, verifying that the file actually exists, and that it is readable."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000378 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000379 "In order to find the directory, the module B<must> be loaded when"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000380 "calling this function."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000381 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000382 "The filename should be a relative path in the format of your local"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000383 "filesystem. It will simply added to the directory using L<File::Spec>'s"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000384 "C<catfile> method."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000385 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000386 "If the file is NOT found for that module, C<class_file> will scan up"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000387 "the module's @ISA tree, looking for the file in all of the parent"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000388 "classes."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000389 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000390 "This allows you to, in effect, \"subclass\" shared files."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000391 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000392 "Returns the file path as a string, or dies if the file or the dist's"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000393 "directory cannot be located, or the file is not readable."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000394 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000395 "=cut"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000396 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000397 "sub class_file"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000398 "{"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000399 "    my $module = _MODULE(shift);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000400 "    my $file   = _FILE(shift);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000401 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000402 "    # Get the super path ( not including UNIVERSAL )"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000403 "    # Rather than using Class::ISA, we'll use an inlined version"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000404 "    # that implements the same basic algorithm."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000405 "    my @path  = ();"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000406 "    my @queue = ($module);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000407 "    my %seen  = ($module => 1);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000408 "    while (my $cl = shift @queue)"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000409 "    {"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000410 "        push @path, $cl;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000411 "        no strict 'refs';    ## no critic (TestingAndDebugging::ProhibitNoStrict)"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000412 "        unshift @queue, grep { !$seen{$_}++ }"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000413 "          map { my $s = $_; $s =~ s/^::/main::/; $s =~ s/\\'/::/g; $s } (@{\"${cl}::ISA\"});"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000414 "    }"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000415 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000416 "    # Search up the path"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000417 "    foreach my $class (@path)"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000418 "    {"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000419 "        my $dir = eval { module_dir($class); };"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000420 "        next if $@;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000421 "        my $path = File::Spec->catfile($dir, $file);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000422 "        -e $path or next;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000423 "        -r $path or Carp::croak(\"File '$file' cannot be read, no read permissions\");"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000424 "        return $path;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000425 "    }"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000426 "    Carp::croak(\"File '$file' does not exist in class or parent shared files\");"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000427 "}"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000428 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000429 "## no critic (BuiltinFunctions::ProhibitStringyEval)"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000430 "if (eval \"use List::MoreUtils 0.428; 1;\")"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000431 "{"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000432 "    List::MoreUtils->import(\"firstres\");"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000433 "}"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000434 "else"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000435 "{"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000436 "    ## no critic (ErrorHandling::RequireCheckingReturnValueOfEval)"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000437 "    eval <<'END_OF_BORROWED_CODE';"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000438 "sub firstres (&@)"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000439 "{"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000440 "    my $test = shift;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000441 "    foreach (@_)"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000442 "    {"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000443 "        my $testval = $test->();"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000444 "        $testval and return $testval;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000445 "    }"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000446 "    return undef;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000447 "}"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000448 "END_OF_BORROWED_CODE"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000449 "}"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000450 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000451 "#####################################################################"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000452 "# Support Functions"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000453 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000454 "sub _search_inc_path"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000455 "{"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000456 "    my $path = shift;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000457 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000458 "    # Find the full dir within @INC"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000459 "    my $dir = firstres("
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000460 "        sub {"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000461 "            my $d;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000462 "            $d = File::Spec->catdir($_, $path) if defined _STRING($_);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000463 "            defined $d and -d $d ? $d : 0;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000464 "        },"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000465 "        @INC"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000466 "    ) or return;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000467 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000468 "    Carp::croak(\"Found directory '$dir', but no read permissions\") unless -r $dir;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000469 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000470 "    return $dir;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000471 "}"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000472 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000473 "sub _module_subdir"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000474 "{"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000475 "    my $module = shift;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000476 "    $module =~ s/::/-/g;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000477 "    return $module;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000478 "}"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000479 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000480 "## no critic (BuiltinFunctions::ProhibitStringyEval)"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000481 "if (eval \"use Params::Util 1.07; 1;\")"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000482 "{"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000483 "    Params::Util->import(\"_CLASS\", \"_STRING\");"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000484 "}"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000485 "else"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000486 "{"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000487 "    ## no critic (ErrorHandling::RequireCheckingReturnValueOfEval)"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000488 "    eval <<'END_OF_BORROWED_CODE';"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000489 "# Inlined from Params::Util pure perl version"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000490 "sub _CLASS ($)"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000491 "{"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000492 "    return (defined $_[0] and !ref $_[0] and $_[0] =~ m/^[^\\W\\d]\\w*(?:::\\w+)*\\z/s) ? $_[0] : undef;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000493 "}"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000494 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000495 "sub _STRING ($)"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000496 "{"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000497 "    (defined $_[0] and ! ref $_[0] and length($_[0])) ? $_[0] : undef;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000498 "}"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000499 "END_OF_BORROWED_CODE"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000500 "}"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000501 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000502 "# Maintainer note: The following private functions are used by"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000503 "#                  File::ShareDir::PAR. (It has to or else it would have to copy&fork)"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000504 "#                  So if you significantly change or even remove them, please"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000505 "#                  notify the File::ShareDir::PAR maintainer(s). Thank you!"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000506 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000507 "# Matches a valid distribution name"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000508 "### This is a total guess at this point"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000509 "sub _DIST    ## no critic (Subroutines::RequireArgUnpacking)"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000510 "{"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000511 "    defined _STRING($_[0]) and $_[0] =~ /^[a-z0-9+_-]+$/is and return $_[0];"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000512 "    Carp::croak(\"Not a valid distribution name\");"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000513 "}"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000514 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000515 "# A valid and loaded module name"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000516 "sub _MODULE"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000517 "{"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000518 "    my $module = _CLASS(shift) or Carp::croak(\"Not a valid module name\");"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000519 "    Class::Inspector->loaded($module) and return $module;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000520 "    Carp::croak(\"Module '$module' is not loaded\");"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000521 "}"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000522 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000523 "# A valid file name"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000524 "sub _FILE"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000525 "{"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000526 "    my $file = shift;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000527 "    _STRING($file) or Carp::croak(\"Did not pass a file name\");"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000528 "    File::Spec->file_name_is_absolute($file) and Carp::croak(\"Cannot use absolute file name '$file'\");"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000529 "    return $file;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000530 "}"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000531 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000532 "1;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000533 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000534 "=pod"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000535 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000536 "=head1 EXTENDING"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000537 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000538 "=head2 Overriding Directory Resolution"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000539 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000540 "C<File::ShareDir> has two convenience hashes for people who have advanced usage"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000541 "requirements of C<File::ShareDir> such as using uninstalled C<share>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000542 "directories during development."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000543 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000544 "  #"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000545 "  # Dist-Name => /absolute/path/for/DistName/share/dir"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000546 "  #"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000547 "  %File::ShareDir::DIST_SHARE"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000548 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000549 "  #"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000550 "  # Module::Name => /absolute/path/for/Module/Name/share/dir"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000551 "  #"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000552 "  %File::ShareDir::MODULE_SHARE"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000553 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000554 "Setting these values any time before the corresponding calls"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000555 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000556 "  dist_dir('Dist-Name')"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000557 "  dist_file('Dist-Name','some/file');"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000558 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000559 "  module_dir('Module::Name');"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000560 "  module_file('Module::Name','some/file');"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000561 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000562 "Will override the base directory for resolving those calls."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000563 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000564 "An example of where this would be useful is in a test for a module that"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000565 "depends on files installed into a share directory, to enable the tests"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000566 "to use the development copy without needing to install them first."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000567 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000568 "  use File::ShareDir;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000569 "  use Cwd qw( getcwd );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000570 "  use File::Spec::Functions qw( rel2abs catdir );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000571 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000572 "  $File::ShareDir::MODULE_SHARE{'Foo::Module'} = rel2abs(catfile(getcwd,'share'));"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000573 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000574 "  use Foo::Module;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000575 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000576 "  # internal calls in Foo::Module to module_file('Foo::Module','bar') now resolves to"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000577 "  # the source trees share/ directory instead of something in @INC"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000578 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000579 "=head1 SUPPORT"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000580 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000581 "Bugs should always be submitted via the CPAN request tracker, see below."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000582 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000583 "You can find documentation for this module with the perldoc command."
