NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000608 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000609 "=head2 Where can I go for other help?"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000610 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000611 "If you have a bug report, a patch or a suggestion, please open a new"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000612 "report ticket at CPAN (but please check previous reports first in case"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000613 "your issue has already been addressed)."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000614 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000615 "Report tickets should contain a detailed description of the bug or"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000616 "enhancement request and at least an easily verifiable way of"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000617 "reproducing the issue or fix. Patches are always welcome, too."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000618 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000619 "=head2 Where can I go for help with a concrete version?"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000620 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000621 "Bugs and feature requests are accepted against the latest version"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000622 "only. To get patches for earlier versions, you need to get an"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000623 "agreement with a developer of your choice - who may or not report the"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000624 "issue and a suggested fix upstream (depends on the license you have"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000625 "chosen)."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000626 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000627 "=head2 Business support and maintenance"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000628 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000629 "For business support you can contact the maintainer via his CPAN"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000630 "email address. Please keep in mind that business support is neither"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000631 "available for free nor are you eligible to receive any support"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000632 "based on the license distributed with this package."
